# CAT2b: If an alarm conveys the same metric via a different sensor, an
# incoming alarm conveying that metric from another sensor can be silenced.
#
# ?alarm is pre-bound by assess.py (the arriving alarm). Reuses
# EVALUATION/CQs/temporal/CQ10_coinciding_equivalence.rq's "technical" branch
# (two independent sensor->signal->analysis->metric traces sharing the same
# Metric TYPE — asserted BACKGROUND/CONDITION facts, no reasoning needed),
# restricted to an already-active prior alarm (see cat2a's header for why
# that needs no extra check here) and — unlike CAT2a — no priority gate: the
# manuscript's own wording for this rule names none.
#
# BOTH ?alarm and ?active required mda:hasCategory alarmcat:Physiological —
# same shared-Signal-particular leak as cat2a_process_priority.rq (see its
# header for the concrete case that surfaced it): a Technical alarm with no
# Metric node of its own can otherwise appear to convey a metric it never
# asserted, merely by sharing a sensor with a coincident physiological one.
#
# ?alarm/?active reach mda:hasSensor straight off mda:triggeredBy, no
# mda:hasFunctionalUnit hop — found necessary here specifically, validating
# against DATA/CAT_evaluation/cat2b_neg (an ECG alarm and an SpO2 alarm on
# ONE PhysiologicalMonitor): assess.py's add_triggered_by targets the
# arriving alarm's own FunctionalUnit particular directly. Going through
# mda:hasFunctionalUnit from the shared device particular instead (an
# earlier version of both this rule and add_triggered_by did) reaches EVERY
# FunctionalUnit that device has ever revealed — for cat2b_neg specifically,
# both the ECG and the SpO2 FU from a single mda:triggeredBy hop, wrongly
# making the ECG alarm's OWN sensor path reachable via the SpO2 FU too, and
# vice versa. See assess.py's add_triggered_by docstring for the full case.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX alarmcat: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/alarm-category/>

SELECT ?active ?metricType WHERE {
  ?alarm mda:hasCategory alarmcat:Physiological .
  ?alarm mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy/mda:hasSensor ?sensorIn .
  ?sensorIn mda:sensorProducesSignal/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?metricIn .
  ?metricIn a ?metricType .

  ?active mda:hasCategory alarmcat:Physiological .
  ?active mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy/mda:hasSensor ?sensorActive .
  ?sensorActive mda:sensorProducesSignal/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?metricActive .
  ?metricActive a ?metricType .

  FILTER(?active != ?alarm)
  FILTER(?sensorActive != ?sensorIn)
}
